    "narrative": "Our strongest plays for today\u2019s slate are anchored by **Tyler Soderstrom** (74.72) and **Mickey Moniak** (74.33). **Tyler Soderstrom** benefits from a massive 10% park boost against Rocker, combined with a favorable R/R platoon edge that elevates his floor significantly. Meanwhile, **Mickey Moniak** is positioned for a high-ceiling performance; the combination of a favorable wind blowing out and a 14% boost from his dynamic platoon split makes him our most efficient start of the day. **Seiya Suzuki** also warrants attention (66.61), as his move into the #2 spot provides enough leverage against Liberatore to warrant a firm recommendation despite the pitcher's moderate xERA.\n\nThe most difficult decision today involved the marginal tier of our infield. **Austin Riley** (62.71) serves as a classic high-reward play despite the unfavorable #8 batting position; the data suggests his high-volume base projection and a slight 2% boost from Pfaadt\u2019s slow delivery\u2014increasing the likelihood of successful stolen base attempts\u2014keeps him firmly in the lineup. Conversely, **Zach McKinstry** (47.81) barely held onto his spot, narrowly edging out our bench depth. While **Jose Caballero** was considered, his lack of a confirmed starting lineup slot rendered him non-viable for our efficiency targets today. We are monitoring the status of **Brice Turang** and **Edwin Arroyo** closely as potential late-inning replacements should the bench clear.\n\nWe must exercise caution regarding the top of the order against elite arms. **Gabriel Moreno** (43.65) and **Corbin Carroll** (52.80) both face a significant penalty for drawing Sale, whose 2.88 xERA is the most daunting matchup on the board. While **Corbin Carroll** remains a priority start due to our organizational emphasis on speed, his output will likely be suppressed by the elite nature of the opposing pitcher. As we navigate the rest of the season, we continue to carry the burden of injuries to **James Wood**, **Vinnie Pasquantino**, and **Giancarlo Stanton**, leaving us with limited flexibility to rotate in **Trevor Story**, **Max Muncy**, or **Dalton Rushing** until they show improved efficiency metrics.",
